closed_decisions:
  - id: DEC-GR-001
    decision: >
      Auditor Session A owns planning, scope freeze, pre-change capture, formal evidence,
      audit verdict, and post-ACCEPT publication. Implementer Session B owns only files
      explicitly allowed by the active phase. The two product task/thread IDs must differ.
  - id: DEC-GR-002
    decision: >
      Auditor Session A may use read-only subagents, but neither Auditor Session A nor any
      of its subagents may implement governance source changes. Implementer Session B may
      not create or edit audit reports, formal EV receipts, verdict receipts, progression
      receipts, LATEST pointers, or plan status projections.
  - id: DEC-GR-003
    decision: >
      Plan approval is a stable external artifact. EXCLUDED plan_registry entries reference
      the stable plan approval decision, never another scope-lock. A phase approval decision
      may reference a scope-lock; the scope-lock must not reference that phase approval.
  - id: DEC-GR-004
    decision: >
      Scope-lock files are immutable and generation-addressed as
      scope-lock-<PHASE>-gNNN.json. A correction creates gNNN+1 with an exact supersedes
      path/hash; no command may rewrite an existing generation.
  - id: DEC-GR-005
    decision: >
      New acceptance artifacts keep the existing v3 schema discriminators and additionally
      require governance_profile audit-governance-recovery/v1. Pre-recovery v3 artifacts
      remain historical inputs and cannot close a new phase.
  - id: DEC-GR-006
    decision: >
      Mechanical producers are mandatory for scope-lock projection, dual-repository state
      capture, EV receipts, audit-report preparation, phase closure, and status publication.
      Manual semantic findings remain an Auditor responsibility; manual cryptographic binding
      or SHA synchronization is forbidden.
  - id: DEC-GR-007
    decision: >
      Producer identity is procedural and structural, not Byzantine-proof cryptographic
      attestation. Each receipt binds an immutable producer-release manifest containing the
      historical tool path, content SHA-256, version, and source base commit; validation never compares an
      old receipt with mutable current tool bytes. Malicious forgery is an explicit non-goal.
  - id: DEC-GR-008
    decision: >
      One workspace-state receipt records both qoderwork and work-one. qoderwork may have a
      frozen pre-existing dirty baseline, but its before/after delta must be contained by the
      phase allowed paths. work-one must remain a clean anchor with no delta.
  - id: DEC-GR-009
    decision: >
      validate-plan must parse the complete phase registry, every registered phase file,
      dependencies, progression status, completion receipt, and 99-final-verification.
      Presence-only checks are forbidden.
  - id: DEC-GR-010
    decision: >
      validate-phase-progression status modes are the only status publication path. Direct
      manual edits of phase status, index status, manifest status, final gates, or the
      registered documents index projection are invalid.
  - id: DEC-GR-011
    decision: >
      close-audit-phase is the single fail-fast closure entrypoint. It executes precheck,
      validate-audit, staged audit publication, staged progression receipt, staged status sync,
      closed-phase progression validation, and plan validation in that exact order, then commits.
      It stops before the next side effect on any failure.
  - id: DEC-GR-012
    decision: >
      Existing M1 audit artifacts are never repaired in place. M1 may be re-baselined only
      after this recovery plan receives an independent final ACCEPT.
  - id: DEC-GR-013
    decision: >
      PHASE-01 has one HUMAN-bound recovery bootstrap waiver because the current admission,
      embedded lock approval, qoderwork state, and status rules cannot authorize their own
      repair. The live index remains BLOCKED until the candidate PHASE-01 audit passes; one
      atomic bootstrap activation/closure then consumes the waiver. It cannot authorize any
      later phase or any manual status edit.
  - id: DEC-GR-014
    decision: >
      Every normal phase follows create scope, run P-02A entry admission, obtain HUMAN approval
      of that exact scope, capture PRE_CHANGE, and only then implement. PHASE-01 replaces only
      the blocked entry-admission result with its exact two-decision waiver; all other order
      constraints remain mandatory.
  - id: DEC-GR-015
    decision: >
      PHASE-01 contains the minimum evidence, report, release, state, and closure producers
      required to audit and adopt itself. Candidate output has no authority until candidate
      validation succeeds and the one-use bootstrap transaction publishes the accepted
      release and receipts. PHASE-02 candidate wrapper may create staged bytes only; accepted
      PHASE-01 validate-phase-progression independently revalidates and commits them through
      its one-use adoption mode. Only PHASE-03 onward invokes the wrapper as accepted tooling.
  - id: DEC-GR-016
    decision: >
      Approval freezes semantic bytes before approval as a content-addressed
      approved-plan-object-set. The checksum manifest contains exactly that object-set entry,
      never mutable live phase paths. After plan approval, one materialization receipt binds
      the approved objects, immutable mirrors, and initial live snapshots. Scope and prewrite
      consume that receipt and immutable mirrors; live plan bytes are never approval identity.
  - id: DEC-GR-017
    decision: >
      Final audit evidence and final publication gates are separate acyclic chains.
      Audit-report evidence is prepared before publication. Ten exclusive final-gate receipts
      are produced at their registered stages and are referenced only by the final status
      authority receipt. That authority receipt is atomically renamed last; its appearance is
      the only FINAL_ACCEPTED event.
  - id: DEC-GR-018
    decision: >
      P0 immutability is an exact 87-file path/SHA manifest covering the seven M1 plan files
      and eighty M1 audit files. P4 is mechanically bounded by a separate approval-bound
      admission contract. The final gate proves no authorized P4 admission or write occurred;
      it does not claim visibility into arbitrary external task-control-plane state.

atomic_requirements:
  - id: REQ-GR-001
    title: Session role separation
    required_behavior: >
      Every active audit bundle binds one immutable session-role manifest containing distinct
      auditor_session_id and implementer_session_id values, role-owned path classes, and the
      HUMAN_USER-approved plan decision.
    observable_result: >
      Missing, equal, unknown, or role-inconsistent session IDs fail with exactly
      SESSION_ROLE_MISSING or SESSION_ROLE_COLLISION.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: component
  - id: REQ-GR-002
    title: Stable approval references
    required_behavior: >
      Every EXCLUDED registry item references the stable plan approval decision path/hash.
      Scope-lock paths and mutable status documents are forbidden approval targets.
    observable_result: >
      A scope-lock approval target fails with APPROVAL_ARTIFACT_UNSTABLE; the stable decision
      fixture passes without any downstream hash rewrite.
    phase: PHASE-03
    evidence_level: component
  - id: REQ-GR-003
    title: Artifact DAG validation
    required_behavior: >
      The shared validator builds the governance JSON reference graph, validates allowed edge
      types, and rejects every directed cycle before audit semantics are evaluated.
    observable_result: >
      A two-node lock cycle fails only ARTIFACT_REFERENCE_CYCLE; a forbidden edge fails only
      ARTIFACT_EDGE_FORBIDDEN; the canonical chain is acyclic.
    phase: PHASE-03
    evidence_level: component
  - id: REQ-GR-004
    title: Immutable versioned scope locks
    required_behavior: >
      prepare-scope-lock creates gNNN with write-exclusive semantics. Existing outputs are
      never overwritten. Later generations require an exact supersedes path/hash and retain
      every prior generation.
    observable_result: >
      Reusing an output path fails SCOPE_LOCK_MUTATION_FORBIDDEN; a broken generation chain
      fails SCOPE_LOCK_GENERATION_INVALID.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-005
    title: Mandatory evidence and report preparation
    required_behavior: >
      EV receipts and the audit contract/report pair are accepted only when produced
      mechanically and their envelope matches an immutable producer-release manifest
      path/hash/version. Auditor findings remain a separate bounded semantic section.
    observable_result: >
      A missing producer envelope fails PRODUCER_METADATA_MISSING and a wrong tool hash or
      dependency/version fails PRODUCER_RELEASE_MISMATCH; an incomplete pair fails
      PREPARED_REPORT_INCOMPLETE.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-006
    title: Dual-repository state receipt
    required_behavior: >
      capture-state reads qoderwork and work-one in one invocation, never mutates scope-lock,
      records both Git roots/HEAD/status/file hashes, and writes a PRE_CHANGE or VERDICT
      receipt with exclusive creation.
    observable_result: >
      Missing either repository fails WORKSPACE_STATE_MISSING; a qoderwork delta outside
      allowed paths or any work-one delta fails WORKSPACE_DELTA_OUT_OF_SCOPE.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-007
    title: Independent execution and domain observations
    required_behavior: >
      EV receipts retain execution.observed/exit_code/timed_out separately from
      domain_observation.result/error_code. Neither value may be inferred from the other.
    observable_result: >
      A command-exit/domain-result disagreement remains representable and is checked against
      its decision case; collapsing the two observations fails the exact receipt contract.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: component
  - id: REQ-GR-008
    title: Complete PLAN_SET admission
    required_behavior: >
      validate-plan checks contiguous manifest order, unique IDs/files, dependency direction,
      phase header equivalence, phase status/receipt consistency, unregistered phase files,
      complete requirement ownership, and 99-final-verification completion.
    observable_result: >
      An empty 99 file, phase/index status split, missing receipt, or unregistered phase file
      fails a stable PLAN_* error and cannot return ok:true.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-009
    title: Admission for every phase and final closure
    required_behavior: >
      validate-phase-progression has distinct entry, closed-phase, and final modes. Entry checks
      the target and dependencies before implementation; closed-phase checks an ACCEPTED staged
      overlay; final checks every phase plus final gates.
    observable_result: >
      No single overall report can project all phases ACCEPTED unless each phase has a valid,
      phase-specific completion receipt.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-010
    title: Sync-only status publication
    required_behavior: >
      validate-phase-progression status modes derive index/phase/99 and the registered
      documents index projection exclusively from validated immutable receipts, use atomic
      writes, record before/after hashes, and refuse free-form target statuses.
    observable_result: >
      An absent/invalid receipt causes zero file changes and STATUS_PUBLICATION_UNAUTHORIZED.
    phase: PHASE-01
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-011
    title: Single closure wrapper
    required_behavior: >
      close-audit-phase executes the eight required closure stages in fixed order, records a
      stage ledger, and performs no later publication after the first nonzero stage.
    observable_result: >
      One isolated stage mutation produces only CLOSURE_STEP_FAILED:<stage>, preserves prior
      evidence, and leaves all later stage effects absent. An injected partial commit produces
      COMMIT_INTERRUPTED and permits only exact journal-bound resume.
    phase: PHASE-02
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-012
    title: Executable conformance verifier
    required_behavior: >
      One table-driven conformance CLI validates file readability, every surface-marker pair,
      three-state negative searches, template discriminators, and ordered failedChecks.
    observable_result: >
      Each isolated missing marker or stale instruction returns exactly one registered
      CONFORMANCE_* failure; unreadable evidence never counts as absence.
    phase: PHASE-04
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-013
    title: Rules, skills, templates, and historical boundary
    required_behavior: >
      AGENTS, provenance rules, planning/audit skills, and active templates state the same role,
      DAG, producer-release, workspace-state, progression, and closure contracts. Historical
      invalid artifacts are explicitly non-repairable.
    observable_result: >
      The PHASE-04 conformance CLI returns ok:true on the active surfaces with no stale v2.1,
      manual-copy, --freeze, or direct-publication instruction.
    phase: PHASE-05
    evidence_level: file-integration
  - id: REQ-GR-014
    title: Documentation and implementation log projection
    required_behavior: >
      After PHASE-01 through PHASE-05 are individually accepted, PHASE-06 writes indexes as
      IMPLEMENTED_PENDING_FINAL_AUDIT and records exact changed surfaces, evidence levels, and
      remaining final-audit gates.
    observable_result: >
      Premature ACCEPTED/COMPLETE language or a missing/misindexed implementation log fails
      PHASE-06 fixed checks and cannot advance final closure.
    phase: PHASE-06
    evidence_level: file-integration

artifact_dag:
  edge_direction: dependent_to_prerequisite
  reference_rule: Every path/SHA or scalar-SHA reference is registered by source kind, field, target kind, and constraint.
  parser_contracts:
    json_reference: "object with exact path and lowercase sha256; both are verified"
    logical_metadata: >
      logical_path, historical_path, live_path, case_set, source_base_commit, profile,
      version, and every field explicitly declared LOGICAL_ONLY are labels, never graph
      references. Parsers may create an edge only from a registered REF field.
    approved_plan_object_set: >
      schema audit-approved-plan-object-set/v1 and kind approved-plan-object-set have exact
      top-level keys schema_version, document_kind, plan_id, generation,
      source_base_commit, entry_count, entries_sha256, entries. Entries are sorted by
      logical_path and cover canonical, PHASE-01..06, and final verification exactly once.
      Each entry has exact keys logical_path, kind, bytes; bytes is a REF to
      approval-objects/sha256/<sha256>. entry_count is 8 and entries_sha256 hashes the UTF-8
      compact JSON entries array. logical_path and source_base_commit are LOGICAL_ONLY.
    checksum_entry: >
      approved-plan-files-r5.sha256 is UTF-8 with exactly one LF-terminated line:
      "<object_set.sha256>  audits/audit-governance-recovery-v1/approved-plan-object-set-r5.json".
      It excludes itself, live plan paths, baselines, requests, decisions, and materialization.
    approved_plan_materialization: >
      schema audit-approved-plan-materialization/v1 and kind approved-plan-materialization
      have exact refs plan_approval, object_set, approved_plan_files, approved_index_baseline;
      semantic_entries contain exactly eight sorted rows with logical_path/kind LOGICAL_ONLY
      plus approved_object, immutable_mirror, and initial_live_snapshot REFs of identical SHA.
      index_entry binds the approved baseline and a content-addressed initial live snapshot.
      semantic_entry_count is 8 and live_path_count is 9. The receipt is exclusive, is created
      after plan approval/materialization, and hashes no later mutable live path.
    frozen_m1_files: >
      schema audit-frozen-file-set/v1 and kind frozen-m1-files contain exactly 87 sorted
      unique entries: seven plans/path-dynamic-resolution-m1 files and eighty
      audits/path-dynamic-resolution-m1 files. Every entry has logical_path LOGICAL_ONLY and
      bytes REF to an immutable object; symlinks, extra/missing paths, and duplicate paths fail.
    p4_boundary_contract: >
      schema audit-p4-boundary/v1 and kind p4-boundary-contract freeze the sole P4 plan ID,
      admission root, plan root, worktree path, admission receipt schema, and prerequisite
      final authority receipt path. All paths are LOGICAL_ONLY. Without the registered
      admission receipt there is no authorized P4 admission or P4 write.
    legacy_bootstrap_repository_receipt: >
      Only PHASE-01 may parse the current schema_version audit-evidence-receipt/v3,
      document_kind evidence-receipt, repository_realpath, phase_id, head, captured_at,
      status_entries, and scalar
      scope_lock_sha256 shape. The scalar must equal the referenced scope bytes. Its
      role is inferred only from the exact approved qoderwork or work-one realpath.
    audit_report_markdown: >
      The only structural outgoing reference is contract; all other structural
      references live in the mechanically generated audit-report-contract.
    projection_snapshot: >
      projection_path is a logical live destination, not a graph reference;
      projection_sha256 must equal bytes.sha256. bytes is the sole path/SHA edge to
      immutable projection-bytes, and sequence is monotonically increasing.
    workspace_state_receipt: >
      Phase form requires scope_lock and phase_approval; final form requires final=true
      and forbids both. Both forms require distinct session roles, producer release,
      exact qoderwork/work-one roots, and PRE_CHANGE or VERDICT kind.
    producer_release_manifest: >
      Exact top-level keys are schema_version, document_kind, governance_profile, release_id,
      case_set, canonical_contract, registry_projection, registry_projection_sha256,
      normalized_source_set_sha256, source_base_commit, producer_version, tool_sources,
      transitive_dependencies, created_at. schema/version/profile are fixed by
      producer_release_registry. Entries are sorted and have exact keys historical_path,
      classification, source_base_commit, version, bytes. historical_path is LOGICAL_ONLY;
      bytes is the only REF and points to objects/sha256/<sha256>. Validation reads only that
      object, never later live historical_path bytes.
    self_kind_edges: >
      scope supersedes and status prior_publication are allowed only when target
      generation or sequence is exactly source minus one; all other self edges fail.
    pending_plan_decision: >
      The pending marker is a true leaf: no path/SHA object, request/baseline reference,
      create_new_path field, or other string interpreted as a governance reference.
    final_gate_receipt: >
      schema final-gate-receipt/v1, kind final-gate-receipt, exclusive output, exact gate ID,
      stage, observed inputs, exit/marker, and registered REFs. Gate receipts are meta-evidence:
      they are excluded from the GATE-005 subject graph and are validated with the final
      authority receipt after GATE-008.
  node_parsers:
    yaml:
      - canonical-requirements
    json:
